sessions.summary:
The game now builds and `npm test` passes (11 of 11). `npm run build` also finishes without errors; its only warning is that the bundle is over 500 kB. The previous run failed because `src/engine/world.js` was still a stub; I've now written it in full to the spec. I haven't opened `npm run dev` or played the game in a browser, so the playability and 60 fps checks haven't been done.

What I changed:
- **`src/engine/world.js`** now meets the full contract:
  - terrain is generated from world coordinates, so there are no seams between chunks;
  - each column has bedrock at the bottom, then stone, then dirt or sand, then grass or sand on top, with water up to sea level;
  - coal (at least one per chunk) and iron ore appear only within their height limits, and trees stay inside their own chunk;
  - chunks are generated when first needed and cached;
  - negative coordinates and blocks above and below the world work as specified;
  - writing a block outside heights 0–63 raises `RangeError`, and putting a block back to its generated value deletes the edit;
  - saving lists edits in a fixed order, so saving a loaded world gives back exactly the same text, and an unknown save version raises an error.
- **Memory fix in `src/render/ChunkRenderer.js`:** it now drops cached chunks far from the player. Without that, the chunks generated next to the visible area would pile up in memory as the player moves. Your edits are kept and reapplied when a chunk is generated again.
- **Bug fix in `src/engine/physics.js`:** with no keys pressed, the player's Z speed came out as `-0` instead of `0`, which strict equality checks in tests treat as a different value.

I also read through the raycast, mesher, inventory, crafting, mining, day/night and block modules against the spec and found nothing else to fix.
